it train, test for calibration\nX_train, X_test, y_train, y_test, sw_train, sw_test = \\\n    train_test_split(X, y, sample_weight, test_size=0.9, random_state=42)\n\n# Gaussian Naive-Bayes with no calibration\nclf = GaussianNB()\nprob_pos_clf = clf.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n\n# Gaussian Naive-Bayes with isotonic calibration\nclf_isotonic = CalibratedClassifierCV(clf, cv=2, method='isotonic')\nprob_pos_isotonic = clf_isotonic.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n\n# Gaussian Naive-Bayes with sigmoid calibration\nclf_sigmoid = CalibratedClassifierCV(clf, cv=2, method='sigmoid')\nprob_pos_sigmoid = clf_sigmoid.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n\nclf_score = brier_score_loss(y_test, prob_pos_clf, sample_weight=sw_test)\n\nclf_isotonic_score = brier_score_loss(y_test, prob_pos_isotonic,\n                                      sample_weight=sw_test)\n\nclf_sigmoid_score = brier_score_loss(y_test, prob_pos_sigmoid,\n                                     sample_weight=sw_test)\ny_unique = np.unique(y)\ncolors = cm.rainbow(np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, y_unique.size))\norder = np.lexsort((prob_pos_clf, ))\n\n```\nHint: Search `examples/calibration/plot_calibration.py` to get the full content if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"plot_calibraton\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/datasets/_base.py:load_digits`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n783 | def load_digits(*, n_class=10, return_X_y=False, as_frame=False):\n784 |     \"\"\"Load and return the digits dataset (classification).\n785 | \n786 |     Each datapoint is a 8x8 image of a digit.\n787 | \n788 |     =================   ==============\n789 |     Classes                         10\n790 |     Samples per class             ~180\n791 |     Samples total                 1797\n792 |     Dimensionality                  64\n793 |     Features             integers 0-16\n794 |     =================   ==============\n795 | \n796 |     Read more in the :ref:`User Guide <digits_dataset>`.\n797 |