or the data X and returns the transformed data.\n1568 | \n1569 |         Parameters\n1570 |         ----------\n1571 |         X : {array-like, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n1572 |             Data matrix to be decomposed\n1573 | \n1574 |         y : Ignored\n1575 | \n1576 |         W : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_components)\n1577 |             If init='custom', it is used as initial guess for the solution.\n1578 | \n1579 |         H : array-like of shape (n_components, n_features)\n1580 |             If init='custom', it is used as initial guess for the solution.\n1581 |             If update_H=False, it is used as a constant, to solve for W only.\n1582 | \n1583 |         update_H : bool, default=True\n1584 |             If True, both W and H will be estimated from initial guesses,\n1585 |             this corresponds to a call to the 'fit_transform' method.\n1586 |             If False, only W will be estimated, this corresponds to a call\n1587 |             to the 'transform' method.\n1588 | \n1589 |         Returns\n1590 |         -------\n1591 |         W : ndarray of shape (n_samples, n_components)\n1592 |             Transformed data.\n1593 | \n1594 |         H : ndarray of shape (n_components, n_features)\n1595 |             Factorization matrix, sometimes called 'dictionary'.\n1596 | \n1597 |         n_iter_ : int\n1598 |             Actual number of iterations.\n1599 |         \"\"\"\n1600 |         check_non_negative(X, \"NMF (input X)\")\n1601 | \n1602 |         # check parameters\n1603 |         self._check_params(X)\n1604 | \n1605 |         if X.min() == 0 and self._beta_loss <= 0:\n1606 |             raise ValueError(\n1607 |                 \"When beta_loss <= 0 and X contains zeros, \"\n1608 |                 \"the solver may diverge. Please add small values \"\n1609 |                 \"to X, or use a positive beta_loss.\"\n1610 |             )\n1611 | \n1612 |         # initialize or check W and H\n1613 |         W, H = se